            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> Are you expecting a no-edit `i` to be special-cased? What do you expect if an edit is done in insert-mode?\n\nI understand your point and now I understand the current behavior...but I have some concerns that might be useful for the discussion.\n\nIMHO when follow mode is disabled, insert should only affect the main cursor.\n\nIn general, follow-mode could be renamed as \"sync-mode\", meaning that when enabled, everithing done by the main cursor is replicated to the other cursors.\n\nThe current behavior is mixed and a little bit confusing: with follow mode disabled, movements aren't replicated but insert/delete/etc. are.",
