            "body": "> when follow mode is disabled, insert should only affect the main cursor.\n\nSo if the user does `<right>` in insert-mode, the other cursors shouldn't follow it? That would result in weird edits. Same for visual-mode: the visual-mode \"motion\" is part of the *user action*, it's not pure motion.\n\n> The current behavior is mixed and a little bit confusing: with follow mode disabled, movements aren't replicated but insert/delete/etc. are.\n\nDeletes are operations. The cursors end up in the place where that operation dictates. Not sure what you are saying here.",
