            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> So if the user does `<right>` in insert-mode, the other cursors shouldn't follow it? That would result in weird edits. Same for visual-mode: the visual-mode \"motion\" is part of the _user action_, it's not pure motion.\n \n> Deletes are operations. The cursors end up in the place where that operation dictates. Not sure what you are saying here.\n\nI'll try to be clearer: I think that from the user's POV an intuitive way for mc to work would be:\n- `follow-mode enabled`: everything is replicated (insert, move, delete, yank, ...).\n- `follow-mode disabled`: nothing is replicated. In this mode one can only add or remove cursors; insert, delete, hjkl, [...], everything affects only main cursor.\n\nThis is why I feel that the current implementation is somewhat inconsistent: with follow-mode disabled, some operations are replicated (e.g. `dw`) while movements are not.\n\nAnd I also find counterintuitive that with `follow-mode disabled`, entering visual mode makes the other cursors starts following the main cursor (if follow-mode is disabled...why are they moving?).\n\n",
