            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> * `follow-mode disabled`: nothing is replicated. In this mode one can only add or remove cursors\n\nIf you want \"nothing replicated\", just delete the cursors (CTRL-L), then hit `gQ` when you want them again.\n\n> with follow-mode disabled, some operations are replicated (e.g. `dw`) while movements are not.\n\nBecause those are operations, not motions. Follow-mode is about motions. \n\n\n> And I also find counterintuitive that with `follow-mode disabled`, entering visual mode makes the other cursors starts following the main cursor (if follow-mode is disabled...why are they moving?).\n\nBecause visual-mode is an operation. The \"motions\" during visual-mode are part of the operation, just like any other operator.",
