            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "It's not a technical distinction, it is a UX distinction. As I mentioned, your \"expected behavior\" of \"do nothing at all\" is already possible by clearing/restoring cursors (`<c-l>`, `gQ`). So if follow-mode is to exist at all, it would land somewhere between that.",
